On ionisation they give different ions

$\begin{array}{c}
{\left[\mathrm{Co}\left(\mathrm{NH}_{3}\right)_{4} \mathrm{Cl}_{2}\right] \mathrm{NO}_{2} \longrightarrow$}$ 
{\left[\mathrm{Co}\left(\mathrm{NH}_{3}\right)_{4} \mathrm{Cl}_{2}\right]^{+}+\mathrm{NO}_{2}^{-}$} \\
{$\left[\mathrm{Co}\left(\mathrm{NH}_{3}\right)_{4} \mathrm{ClNO}_{2}\right] \mathrm{Cl} \longrightarrow$} 
{$\left[\mathrm{Co}\left(\mathrm{NH}_{3}\right)_{4} \mathrm{CINO}_{2}\right]^{+}+\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$}
\end{array}

So, they show ionisation isomerism.

