$\text{$ The $cis and trans both form of complex } \left[M\left(\mathrm{NH}_3\right)_4 \mathrm{Cl}_2\right]\text{$ are optically inactive }
There are plane of symmetry in addition to that there is alternate axis of symmetry  $\left(C_n\right)$ which also causes their optical inactivity.
A molecule possesses $n$ fold alternating axis of symmetry, if when rotated through an angle of $360^{{}^{\circ}} / \mathrm{n}$ about the axis and then followed by reflection in a plane perpendicular to the axis, the molecule is indistinguishable from the original molecule.

